# The repository stores LF for everything it decides is text. Line endings in a working
# tree are then the platform's business and never the diff's.
#
# Without this the repository was mixed with no rule behind it -- README.md, Common.ps1,
# Land.ps1 and the skills were CRLF; Audit.ps1, Lane.ps1, Prove-Gate.ps1 and the gate checks
# were LF -- so an editor or a script that wrote the other kind turned a two-line change into
# a whole-file diff, and the real edit was unreviewable inside it. That happened.
#
# `auto` rather than a list: git detects binary content and leaves it alone, so nothing has
# to be enumerated ahead of being added.
* text=auto
